{
  "id": "wulfic-keyword-prime-layer-grid",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Keywords paired with prime-derived streams",
  "reader_title": "Can combining a keyword and a number sequence decode the pages?",
  "reader_intro": "Adds or subtracts a repeating keyword together with one of 103 fixed number sequences, including primes, counting and Fibonacci numbers, then checks how often the output runes repeat.",
  "question": "Does any source-specified keyword and prime-derived stream combination lift LP2 page text above the archived IoC candidate screen?",
  "reader_question": "Could a keyword and a prime stream remove two cipher layers?",
  "summary": "An adapted test of a pinned archived source grid found no setting above its IoC screen on the correctly mapped LP2 pages.",
  "finding": "Across 224,128 keyword/stream/sign/page settings on LP2-04–37, none scored above the source IoC>1.40 screen. The maximum was 1.2902 on LP2-32. A 515-rune established reading encrypted with one declared setting was recovered exactly and scored 1.7231. In 49 seeded page-wise shuffle controls repeating the full search, 42 reached a maximum at least as high as the LP2 maximum.",
  "limitations": "This is the exact finite source grid adapted to verified current text, not a replay of the archived script’s old results. Its directory and page-number assumptions were outdated; old page_21–54 means current LP2-04–37. A prior wrong-target exploratory run was discarded and documented. The 515-rune positive control is longer than any target page, so it does not establish equal power on short pages. IoC is not a language detector; 49 shuffles preserve page histograms but do not model every cipher. Other keywords, stream rules, phases, boundaries or layers remain outside scope. Keyword labels refer to literal source numeric arrays; the AETHEREAL array includes an extra H after TH, so a conventional re-encoding is not covered.",
  "next_steps": "A related claim should specify both complete key streams and the page boundary/reset rule, then show a full reading that survives a whole-search comparison and a planted control.",
  "outcome": "not-supported",
